# Security Review Checklist

> Security level: {{SECURITY_LEVEL}} | Compliance: {{COMPLIANCE_REQS}}

## Pre-Review
- [ ] Know the security context (above)
- [ ] Have codebase access

## OWASP Top 10

### A01: Access Control
- [ ] All endpoints check auth
- [ ] Users access only their data
- [ ] Admin functions protected

### A02: Cryptography
- [ ] No hardcoded secrets
- [ ] TLS/HTTPS enforced
- [ ] Passwords hashed (bcrypt/argon2)

### A03: Injection
- [ ] SQL parameterized
- [ ] No eval() on user input
- [ ] HTML escaped (XSS)

### A04-A05: Design & Config
- [ ] Security headers set
- [ ] No default credentials
- [ ] Errors don't leak info

### A06: Components
- [ ] npm audit clean
- [ ] No known CVEs

## Credentials Security

- [ ] No `.env` files in repository
- [ ] No hardcoded secrets in source code
- [ ] All secrets use `process.env.VARIABLE_NAME`
- [ ] `.env.example` documents all required variables
- [ ] Sensitive env vars validated at startup
- [ ] No secrets in logs or error messages
- [ ] API keys have minimum required permissions
- [ ] Secrets rotation schedule documented

### A07-A10: Auth & Logging
- [ ] Session management secure
- [ ] Security events logged
- [ ] External URLs validated

